      {
        "id": "E3",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Together, these optimizations reduced token consumption by up to 71% and cut average latency by up to 80% across our benchmark runs on a representative 23 MB payload.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E4",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "In Figure 1, the Optimizer receives a Request JSON and produces a Response JSON, which is then validated by a Business Rules Validator to generate a Validation Report JSON.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E5",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The agent uses an Amazon Bedrock model for reasoning and Amazon Bedrock AgentCore memory , a capability of Amazon Bedrock AgentCore, to persist chat interactions across turns, and each turn follows this flow (Figure 2):",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E6",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We implemented three strategies to reduce the token costs, latency, and memory overhead caused by passing large JSON payloads through the model context.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E7",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "When a tool returns an oversized list or dictionary, the agent stores the full result in Amazon Simple Storage Service (Amazon S3) and passes the model a compact summary with a handle.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E8",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "Amazon Bedrock AgentCore with Amazon Bedrock AgentCore memory enabled for session-state persistence.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E9",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We therefore moved heavy artifacts (request JSON, response JSON, validation data, and other large derived payloads) to Amazon S3.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E10",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The S3-backed store exposes a put_json and get_json interface.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E11",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "The S3ArtifactStore class wraps the put_json / get_json interface with an in-process cache and content-addressed keys:",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
        "source": "AWS Machine Learning Blog",
        "publishedAt": "2026-11-17T22:44:51.000Z",
        "checkedAt": "2026-11-18T03:41:03.773Z"
      },
      {
        "id": "E12",
        "kind": "body",
        "text": "We then compared token usage and latency in Amazon Bedrock AgentCore Observability (a capability of AgentCore), and observed clear improvements in both cost and responsiveness.",
        "sourceUrl": "https://aws.amazon.com/blogs/machine-learning/reducing-token-costs-and-latency-in-amazon-bedrock-agentcore-json-workloads/",
